          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Exhibitions and Recognition</strong><br>\nThroughout her life, O'Keeffe was the subject of major exhibitions and received numerous accolades for her work, establishing her as a central figure in American art. She was a pioneer among women in the arts, recognized for her unique vision.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Later Years and Legacy</strong><br>\nO'Keeffe continued to create art late into her life, despite vision problems in her old age. Her legacy is preserved at the Georgia O'Keeffe Museum in Santa Fe, which houses a significant collection of her work and materials related to her life.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Posthumous Fame</strong><br>\nGeorgia O'Keeffe passed away in 1986 at the age of 98. Her life's work left an indelible mark on the art world, with her paintings remaining highly regarded for their originality and enduring influence on subsequent generations of artists.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
